# Key Concepts Demonstrated

### Infrastructure as Code

Terraform is used to provision and manage AWS infrastructure through configuration files.

### Configuration Management

Ansible is used to configure multiple EC2 servers and deploy the application consistently.

### Containerization

Docker packages the Flask application and its dependencies into a portable container image.

### Container Registry

Docker Hub stores the application image so that the EC2 instances can pull and deploy it.

### Multi-Server Deployment

The same application is deployed to two independent EC2 instances using a single Ansible playbook.

### SSH-Based Automation

Ansible connects to the EC2 instances through SSH and performs the required configuration and deployment tasks.

### Infrastructure → Configuration → Application

```text
Terraform
   ↓
AWS Infrastructure
   ↓
Ansible
   ↓
Server Configuration
   ↓
Docker
   ↓
Application Deployment
```
